This revised code uses a regular `Map` object instead of a `WeakMap`, storing the calculated color results by the image file name. This allows for reusing the calculated values between different instances of the same image, reducing redundant calculations. The `getBackgroundForImage` function checks if the result is already cached and calculates it if not, then returns the cached result. This approach simplifies the management of the cache and avoids unnecessary Vue reactivity overhead.

